import VOA.Examples.AffineSl2VOAInstance
import VOA.Modules.PoissonDescent

/-!
# The symbol of the weight-3 singular vector of `V^{-4/3}(𝔰𝔩₂)` in `A₂`

`Examples/AffineSl2Singular` produces the weight-3, charge-2 singular vector

```
s = 20·M1 − 12·M2 − 6·M3 + 36·M4 + 9·M5     at k = -4/3,
M1 = e₋₃|0⟩, M2 = e₋₂h₋₁|0⟩, M3 = h₋₂e₋₁|0⟩, M4 = e₋₁e₋₁f₋₁|0⟩, M5 = e₋₁h₋₁h₋₁|0⟩.
```

This file computes the image (the **symbol**) of `s` in the Poisson algebra
`A₂(𝒱) = 𝒱 ⧸ O₂(𝒱)` of `Modules.C2Cofinite` / `Modules.PoissonDescent`, where
`O₂(𝒱) = span{u₍₋₂₎v}` and the commutative product is `[u]·[v] = [u₍₋₁₎v]` (`A₂CommRing`).

## The mechanism

The one nontrivial input is that a current mode of index `≤ -2` kills anything modulo `O₂`.  Note
that the weaker statement `T𝒱 ⊆ O₂` is *not* enough for this; what is used is the **operator**
form, available because `O₂` is spanned by `u₍₋₂₎v` for *arbitrary* `v`:

* `Modules/PoissonDescent.smul_le_neg_two_mem_O₂` gives `W.smul u n v ∈ O₂ W` for every `n ≤ -2`
  and every `u, v`;
* `Examples/AffineSl2VOAInstance.smul_currentState_eq_J` identifies the VOA mode of the current
  state with the affine mode, `(Jᵃ₋₁|0⟩)₍ₙ₎ = Jᵃₙ`.

Composing them is `J_mem_O₂`: `Jᵃₙ v ∈ O₂` for `n ≤ -2`, *any* `v`.  Dually, a monomial built
purely from `₍₋₁₎`-modes of current states *is* an iterated Poisson product, since
`currentState k a = Jᵃ₋₁|0⟩` and `poissonMul W u v = u₍₋₁₎v`; that is `M4_eq_poissonMul` and
`M5_eq_poissonMul`, which are proved by `simp only` from the two bridge lemmas and hold on the
nose (no `O₂` correction).

So `M1, M2, M3` die and

```
[s] = 36·[e]([e][f]) + 9·[e]([h][h]) = 9·[e]·(4[e][f] + [h]²),
```

the last factor being the classical `𝔰𝔩₂` Casimir in this repository's normalisation
(`⁅e,f⁆ = h`, `κ(e,f) = 1`, `κ(h,h) = 2`), i.e. the defining equation `h² + 4ef = 0` of the
nilpotent cone `𝒩 ⊂ 𝔰𝔩₂`.

§4 checks that the Poisson bracket on the three classes really is the Kirillov–Kostant bracket of
`𝔰𝔩₂` and that `4[e][f] + [h]²` is central for it — so the ideal it generates is a Poisson ideal.

## Main results

* `J_mem_O₂` — the mode-death lemma: `Jᵃₙ v ∈ O₂` for `n ≤ -2`, any `v`.  The crux.
* `M1_mem_O₂`, `M2_mem_O₂`, `M3_mem_O₂`; `mk₂_M1`, `mk₂_M2`, `mk₂_M3` (the classes vanish).
* `M4_eq_poissonMul`, `M5_eq_poissonMul`; `mk₂_M4 : [M4] = [e]·([e]·[f])`,
  `mk₂_M5 : [M5] = [e]·([h]·[h])`.
* `mk₂_ansatz` — the symbol of the *general* weight-3 charge-2 ansatz at *every* non-critical
  level: `[a M1 + b M2 + c M3 + d M4 + g M5] = d·[e]([e][f]) + g·[e]([h][h])`.
* `mk₂_sl2Singular` — `[s] = 36·[e]([e][f]) + 9·[e]([h][h])`.
* `mk₂_sl2Singular_casimir` — `[s] = 9·[e]·(4[e][f] + [h]²)`, the Casimir factorisation.
* `A₂bracket_e_f`, `A₂bracket_h_e`, `A₂bracket_h_f` — `⁅[e],[f]⁆ = [h]`, `⁅[h],[e]⁆ = 2[e]`,
  `⁅[h],[f]⁆ = -2[f]`: the Poisson bracket on the classes is the `𝔰𝔩₂` bracket.
* `A₂bracket_e_casimir`, `A₂bracket_f_casimir`, `A₂bracket_h_casimir` — the Casimir class is
  central, so `(casimirCl)` is a Poisson ideal of the subalgebra generated by `[e], [f], [h]`.

## Status

`sorry`-free and **axiom-clean**: every declaration reports exactly
`[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]` (see the `AxiomAudit` section at the end).  In
particular nothing here uses the theorem `VOA.pbw`.

⚠ **What is deliberately NOT established.**

* **No nonvanishing, and `A₂` itself is not shown nonzero.**  Nothing here proves `[s] ≠ 0`, nor
  `[e] ≠ 0`, nor `A₂(V^{-4/3}(𝔰𝔩₂)) ≠ 0`, nor that `[e], [f], [h]` are algebraically
  independent.  Proving `R_{V^k(𝔰𝔩₂)} ≅ ℂ[e,f,h]` (the polynomial ring on the three classes)
  needs a PBW-type input; this file does not use one.  (Elsewhere: `[s]`'s representative is
  nonzero, `Wak.sl2Singular_ne_zero`; PBW for `V^k(𝔰𝔩₂)`, `k + 2 ≠ 0`, is
  `AffineSl2WakimotoLiLeading.affineSl2PBWBasis`, and injectivity of the symbol map follows via
  `AffineSl2PBWWakimotoReduction.symbolAlg_injective_of_wakimotoOrderedCreationState_linearIndependent`
  with `AffineSl2WakimotoLiLeading.wakimotoOrderedCreationState_linearIndependent`.)  Every
  statement below is an identity between classes, true even in the degenerate case.
* **No associated variety.**  These are computations in `A₂` of the **universal** VOA
  `V^{-4/3}(𝔰𝔩₂)`, not of the **simple quotient** `L_{-4/3}(𝔰𝔩₂)`.  The statement
  `R_{L_{-4/3}(𝔰𝔩₂)} = ℂ[e,f,h]/(h²+4ef) = ℂ[𝒩]` — hence quasi-lisse but not lisse — additionally
  requires a presentation of `A₂` of the quotient VOA (the image of `O₂` under the quotient map,
  plus the Poisson ideal generated by the symbol).  That is not attempted here.
* **No relation between `A₂` and `Sym(𝔰𝔩₂)`.**  The repository contains no lemma identifying
  `A₂(V^k(𝔤))` with `ℂ[𝔤*]`; the images are computed as classes, and the "polynomial" reading of
  `36 e²f + 9 e h²` is commentary, not a theorem.

## References
* Gannon §5.3.2 (the Poisson algebra `A₂`); Zhu; Arakawa–Kawasetsu (quasi-lisse).
* `Modules/C2Cofinite`, `Modules/PoissonDescent`, `Examples/AffineSl2Singular`,
  `Examples/AffineSl2VOAInstance`.
-/

namespace VOA.Sl2Symbol

open VOA
open VOA.AffineVOA
open VOA.AffineVOA.Inst
open VertexOperatorAlgebra

universe u

/-! ## §0  Scalars versus the descended product

`A₂mul` is a `ℂ`-bilinear map and the `CommRing` multiplication of `A₂CommRing` is
*definitionally* `A₂mul`; but the repository registers no `Algebra ℂ (A₂ W)` (hence no
`SMulCommClass`), so the scalar/product interchange has to be named by hand. -/

section Generic

variable {𝒱 : Type u} [AddCommGroup 𝒱] [Module ℂ 𝒱]

/-- Scalars pass through the descended product on the right: `p · (c • q) = c • (p · q)`. -/
theorem A₂_mul_smul (W : VertexOperatorAlgebra 𝒱) (c : ℂ) (p q : A₂ W) :
    p * (c • q) = c • (p * q) :=
  map_smul (A₂mul W p) c q

/-- Scalars pass through the descended product on the left: `(c • p) · q = c • (p · q)`. -/
theorem A₂_smul_mul (W : VertexOperatorAlgebra 𝒱) (c : ℂ) (p q : A₂ W) :
    (c • p) * q = c • (p * q) := by
  have h : A₂mul W (c • p) = c • A₂mul W p := map_smul (A₂mul W) c p
  calc (c • p) * q = A₂mul W (c • p) q := rfl
    _ = (c • A₂mul W p) q := by rw [h]
    _ = c • A₂mul W p q := LinearMap.smul_apply _ _ _
    _ = c • (p * q) := rfl

end Generic

variable (k : ℂ) (hk : k + 2 ≠ 0)

/-! ## §1  Every current mode of index `≤ -2` lands in `O₂`

⚠ This is the crux of the whole file.  It is *not* obtained from `T𝒱 ⊆ O₂`; it is the operator
statement, which is available because `O₂ = span{u₍₋₂₎v}` ranges over **arbitrary** `v` — so it
suffices to know that the affine mode `Jᵃₙ` *is* a VOA mode of a state, which is
`smul_currentState_eq_J`. -/

/-- **The mode-death lemma.**  For `n ≤ -2` and *any* `v`, the affine current mode `Jᵃₙ v` lies
in `O₂ = span{u₍₋₂₎w}`, because `Jᵃₙ v = (Jᵃ₋₁|0⟩)₍ₙ₎v` and every VOA mode of index `≤ -2`
lands in `O₂` (`smul_le_neg_two_mem_O₂`). -/
theorem J_mem_O₂ (a : Fin 3) {n : ℤ} (hn : n ≤ -2) (v : WakModule k) :
    J k a n v ∈ O₂ (affineSl2VOA_closed k hk) := by
  rw [← smul_currentState_eq_J k hk a n v]
  exact smul_le_neg_two_mem_O₂ _ _ _ hn

/-- `M1 = e₋₃|0⟩ ∈ O₂` (outer mode `-3 ≤ -2`). -/
theorem M1_mem_O₂ : Sl2Sing.M1 k ∈ O₂ (affineSl2VOA_closed k hk) := by
  rw [Sl2Sing.M1_def]
  exact J_mem_O₂ k hk colE (by norm_num) _

/-- `M2 = e₋₂h₋₁|0⟩ ∈ O₂` (outer mode `-2`). -/
theorem M2_mem_O₂ : Sl2Sing.M2 k ∈ O₂ (affineSl2VOA_closed k hk) := by
  rw [Sl2Sing.M2_def]
  exact J_mem_O₂ k hk colE (by norm_num) _

/-- `M3 = h₋₂e₋₁|0⟩ ∈ O₂` (outer mode `-2`). -/
theorem M3_mem_O₂ : Sl2Sing.M3 k ∈ O₂ (affineSl2VOA_closed k hk) := by
  rw [Sl2Sing.M3_def]
  exact J_mem_O₂ k hk colH (by norm_num) _

/-! ## §2  The three current classes, and the two surviving monomials as products -/

/-- The class `[e] = [e₋₁|0⟩] ∈ A₂`. -/
noncomputable def eCl : A₂ (affineSl2VOA_closed k hk) :=
  mk₂ (affineSl2VOA_closed k hk) (currentState k colE)

/-- The class `[f] = [f₋₁|0⟩] ∈ A₂`. -/
noncomputable def fCl : A₂ (affineSl2VOA_closed k hk) :=
  mk₂ (affineSl2VOA_closed k hk) (currentState k colF)

/-- The class `[h] = [h₋₁|0⟩] ∈ A₂`. -/
noncomputable def hCl : A₂ (affineSl2VOA_closed k hk) :=
  mk₂ (affineSl2VOA_closed k hk) (currentState k colH)

/-- `M4 = e₋₁e₋₁f₋₁|0⟩` is *literally* — before any quotient — the iterated Poisson product
`e₍₋₁₎(e₍₋₁₎f)` of the current states. -/
theorem M4_eq_poissonMul :
    Sl2Sing.M4 k
      = poissonMul (affineSl2VOA_closed k hk) (currentState k colE)
          (poissonMul (affineSl2VOA_closed k hk) (currentState k colE) (currentState k colF)) := by
  simp only [poissonMul_def, smul_currentState_eq_J]
  simp only [currentState_def, Sl2Sing.M4_def]

/-- `M5 = e₋₁h₋₁h₋₁|0⟩` is *literally* the iterated Poisson product `e₍₋₁₎(h₍₋₁₎h)`. -/
theorem M5_eq_poissonMul :
    Sl2Sing.M5 k
      = poissonMul (affineSl2VOA_closed k hk) (currentState k colE)
          (poissonMul (affineSl2VOA_closed k hk) (currentState k colH) (currentState k colH)) := by
  simp only [poissonMul_def, smul_currentState_eq_J]
  simp only [currentState_def, Sl2Sing.M5_def]

/-- The class of `M4` is the ring product `[e]·([e]·[f])`. -/
theorem mk₂_M4 :
    mk₂ (affineSl2VOA_closed k hk) (Sl2Sing.M4 k)
      = eCl k hk * (eCl k hk * fCl k hk) := by
  rw [eCl, fCl, A₂_mul_mk, A₂_mul_mk, M4_eq_poissonMul k hk]

/-- The class of `M5` is the ring product `[e]·([h]·[h])`. -/
theorem mk₂_M5 :
    mk₂ (affineSl2VOA_closed k hk) (Sl2Sing.M5 k)
      = eCl k hk * (hCl k hk * hCl k hk) := by
  rw [eCl, hCl, A₂_mul_mk, A₂_mul_mk, M5_eq_poissonMul k hk]

/-! ## §3  The symbol of the general ansatz, and of `sl2Singular` -/

/-- `[M1] = 0` in `A₂`. -/
theorem mk₂_M1 : mk₂ (affineSl2VOA_closed k hk) (Sl2Sing.M1 k) = 0 :=
  (mk₂_eq_zero_iff _).mpr (M1_mem_O₂ k hk)

/-- `[M2] = 0` in `A₂`. -/
theorem mk₂_M2 : mk₂ (affineSl2VOA_closed k hk) (Sl2Sing.M2 k) = 0 :=
  (mk₂_eq_zero_iff _).mpr (M2_mem_O₂ k hk)

/-- `[M3] = 0` in `A₂`. -/
theorem mk₂_M3 : mk₂ (affineSl2VOA_closed k hk) (Sl2Sing.M3 k) = 0 :=
  (mk₂_eq_zero_iff _).mpr (M3_mem_O₂ k hk)

/-- **The symbol of the general weight-3 charge-2 ansatz**, at every non-critical level.  The
three monomials carrying a mode of index `≤ -2` die; only the two pure `₍₋₁₎`-monomials survive,
as `[e]([e][f])` and `[e]([h][h])`. -/
theorem mk₂_ansatz (a b c d g : ℂ) :
    mk₂ (affineSl2VOA_closed k hk) (Sl2Sing.ansatz k a b c d g)
      = d • (eCl k hk * (eCl k hk * fCl k hk))
        + g • (eCl k hk * (hCl k hk * hCl k hk)) := by
  rw [Sl2Sing.ansatz_def]
  simp only [map_add, map_smul, mk₂_M1, mk₂_M2, mk₂_M3, mk₂_M4, mk₂_M5, smul_zero,
    zero_add, add_zero]

/-- The classical `𝔰𝔩₂` **Casimir** `4ef + h²`, as an element of `A₂`.  With this repository's
normalisation (`⁅e,f⁆ = h`, `κ(e,f) = 1`, `κ(h,h) = 2`) the vanishing of `h² + 4ef` is the
defining equation of the nilpotent cone `𝒩 ⊂ 𝔰𝔩₂` (`det [[h/2, e],[f, -h/2]] = 0`). -/
noncomputable def casimirCl : A₂ (affineSl2VOA_closed k hk) :=
  (4 : ℂ) • (eCl k hk * fCl k hk) + hCl k hk * hCl k hk

/-- **The Casimir factorisation, at every non-critical level.**  Expanding the product
`9·[e]·(4[e][f] + [h]²)` reproduces `36·[e]([e][f]) + 9·[e]([h][h])`. -/
theorem smul_casimir_expand :
    (9 : ℂ) • (eCl k hk * casimirCl k hk)
      = (36 : ℂ) • (eCl k hk * (eCl k hk * fCl k hk))
        + (9 : ℂ) • (eCl k hk * (hCl k hk * hCl k hk)) := by
  rw [casimirCl, mul_add, A₂_mul_smul, smul_add, smul_smul]
  norm_num

/-! ### §3.1  Specialisation to the admissible level `k = -4/3` -/

/-- `V^{-4/3}(𝔰𝔩₂)`; reducibly equal to `Inst.voaSl2Adm`. -/
noncomputable abbrev Wadm : VertexOperatorAlgebra (WakModule (-4 / 3 : ℂ)) :=
  affineSl2VOA_closed (-4 / 3 : ℂ) admLevel_noncritical

/-- `[e]` at `k = -4/3`, in `A₂(V^{-4/3}(𝔰𝔩₂))`. -/
noncomputable abbrev eA : A₂ Wadm := eCl (-4 / 3 : ℂ) admLevel_noncritical

/-- `[f]` at `k = -4/3`. -/
noncomputable abbrev fA : A₂ Wadm := fCl (-4 / 3 : ℂ) admLevel_noncritical

/-- `[h]` at `k = -4/3`. -/
noncomputable abbrev hA : A₂ Wadm := hCl (-4 / 3 : ℂ) admLevel_noncritical

/-- The Casimir class `4[e][f] + [h]²` at `k = -4/3`. -/
noncomputable abbrev casimirA : A₂ Wadm := casimirCl (-4 / 3 : ℂ) admLevel_noncritical

/-- **The symbol of the weight-3 singular vector**, expanded:
`[s] = 36·[e]([e][f]) + 9·[e]([h][h])`, i.e. `36 e²f + 9 e h²`. -/
theorem mk₂_sl2Singular :
    mk₂ Wadm Sl2Sing.sl2Singular
      = (36 : ℂ) • (eA * (eA * fA)) + (9 : ℂ) • (eA * (hA * hA)) := by
  rw [Sl2Sing.sl2Singular_def]
  exact mk₂_ansatz (-4 / 3 : ℂ) admLevel_noncritical 20 (-12) (-6) 36 9

/-- **The Casimir factorisation of the symbol**: `[s] = 9 · [e] · (4[e][f] + [h]²)`, i.e.
`9 e (4ef + h²)` — nine times the coordinate `e` times the classical `𝔰𝔩₂` Casimir. -/
theorem mk₂_sl2Singular_casimir :
    mk₂ Wadm Sl2Sing.sl2Singular = (9 : ℂ) • (eA * casimirA) := by
  rw [mk₂_sl2Singular]
  exact (smul_casimir_expand (-4 / 3 : ℂ) admLevel_noncritical).symm

/-- The same statement phrased with the packaged instance `Inst.voaSl2Adm`. -/
theorem mk₂_sl2Singular_casimir_voaSl2Adm :
    mk₂ voaSl2Adm Sl2Sing.sl2Singular = (9 : ℂ) • (eA * casimirA) :=
  mk₂_sl2Singular_casimir

/-! ## §4  The Poisson bracket on the classes is the `𝔰𝔩₂` bracket, and the Casimir is central

The product side above says nothing about the Lie side.  Here we check the bracket
`⁅[u],[v]⁆ = [u₍₀₎v]` (`A₂bracket`) on the three classes, and deduce that the Casimir class is
central — so the ideal it generates is a **Poisson** ideal, which is what makes the associated
variety of the quotient a union of coadjoint (nilpotent) orbits. -/

/-- Representative computation: `e₍₀₎f = h₋₁|0⟩`. -/
theorem poissonBracket_e_f :
    poissonBracket (affineSl2VOA_closed k hk) (currentState k colE) (currentState k colF)
      = currentState k colH := by
  rw [poissonBracket_def, smul_currentState_eq_J]
  simp only [currentState_def]
  exact Sl2Sing.E0F1 k

/-- Representative computation: `h₍₀₎e = 2 e₋₁|0⟩`. -/
theorem poissonBracket_h_e :
    poissonBracket (affineSl2VOA_closed k hk) (currentState k colH) (currentState k colE)
      = (2 : ℂ) • currentState k colE := by
  rw [poissonBracket_def, smul_currentState_eq_J]
  simp only [currentState_def]
  rw [Sl2Sing.HEs k 0 (-1) (-1) (by norm_num), Sl2Sing.H_vac0, map_zero, zero_add]

/-- Representative computation: `h₍₀₎f = -2 f₋₁|0⟩`. -/
theorem poissonBracket_h_f :
    poissonBracket (affineSl2VOA_closed k hk) (currentState k colH) (currentState k colF)
      = (-2 : ℂ) • currentState k colF := by
  rw [poissonBracket_def, smul_currentState_eq_J]
  simp only [currentState_def]
  rw [Sl2Sing.HFs k 0 (-1) (-1) (by norm_num), Sl2Sing.H_vac0, map_zero, zero_sub]
  module

/-- `⁅[e],[f]⁆ = [h]`. -/
theorem A₂bracket_e_f :
    A₂bracket (affineSl2VOA_closed k hk) (eCl k hk) (fCl k hk) = hCl k hk := by
  rw [eCl, fCl, hCl, A₂bracket_mk, poissonBracket_e_f k hk]

/-- `⁅[h],[e]⁆ = 2[e]`. -/
theorem A₂bracket_h_e :
    A₂bracket (affineSl2VOA_closed k hk) (hCl k hk) (eCl k hk) = (2 : ℂ) • eCl k hk := by
  rw [eCl, hCl, A₂bracket_mk, poissonBracket_h_e k hk, map_smul]

/-- `⁅[h],[f]⁆ = -2[f]`. -/
theorem A₂bracket_h_f :
    A₂bracket (affineSl2VOA_closed k hk) (hCl k hk) (fCl k hk) = (-2 : ℂ) • fCl k hk := by
  rw [fCl, hCl, A₂bracket_mk, poissonBracket_h_f k hk, map_smul]

/-- `⁅[e],[h]⁆ = -2[e]` (antisymmetry). -/
theorem A₂bracket_e_h :
    A₂bracket (affineSl2VOA_closed k hk) (eCl k hk) (hCl k hk) = (-2 : ℂ) • eCl k hk := by
  rw [A₂bracket_antisymm, A₂bracket_h_e k hk]
  module

/-- `⁅[f],[h]⁆ = 2[f]` (antisymmetry). -/
theorem A₂bracket_f_h :
    A₂bracket (affineSl2VOA_closed k hk) (fCl k hk) (hCl k hk) = (2 : ℂ) • fCl k hk := by
  rw [A₂bracket_antisymm, A₂bracket_h_f k hk]
  module

/-- `⁅[f],[e]⁆ = -[h]` (antisymmetry). -/
theorem A₂bracket_f_e :
    A₂bracket (affineSl2VOA_closed k hk) (fCl k hk) (eCl k hk) = -hCl k hk := by
  rw [A₂bracket_antisymm, A₂bracket_e_f k hk]

/-- **The Casimir class is central**: `⁅[e], 4[e][f] + [h]²⁆ = 0`. -/
theorem A₂bracket_e_casimir :
    A₂bracket (affineSl2VOA_closed k hk) (eCl k hk) (casimirCl k hk) = 0 := by
  have hef : A₂bracket (affineSl2VOA_closed k hk) (eCl k hk) (eCl k hk * fCl k hk)
      = eCl k hk * hCl k hk := by
    rw [show (eCl k hk * fCl k hk) = A₂mul (affineSl2VOA_closed k hk) (eCl k hk) (fCl k hk)
        from rfl, A₂_leibniz, A₂bracket_self, A₂bracket_e_f k hk, map_zero,
      LinearMap.zero_apply, zero_add]
    rfl
  have hhh : A₂bracket (affineSl2VOA_closed k hk) (eCl k hk) (hCl k hk * hCl k hk)
      = (-4 : ℂ) • (eCl k hk * hCl k hk) := by
    rw [show (hCl k hk * hCl k hk) = A₂mul (affineSl2VOA_closed k hk) (hCl k hk) (hCl k hk)
        from rfl, A₂_leibniz, A₂bracket_e_h k hk]
    change (-2 : ℂ) • eCl k hk * hCl k hk + hCl k hk * ((-2 : ℂ) • eCl k hk)
      = (-4 : ℂ) • (eCl k hk * hCl k hk)
    rw [A₂_smul_mul, A₂_mul_smul, mul_comm (hCl k hk) (eCl k hk)]
    module
  rw [casimirCl, map_add, map_smul, hef, hhh]
  module

/-- `⁅[f], 4[e][f] + [h]²⁆ = 0`. -/
theorem A₂bracket_f_casimir :
    A₂bracket (affineSl2VOA_closed k hk) (fCl k hk) (casimirCl k hk) = 0 := by
  have hef : A₂bracket (affineSl2VOA_closed k hk) (fCl k hk) (eCl k hk * fCl k hk)
      = (-1 : ℂ) • (hCl k hk * fCl k hk) := by
    rw [show (eCl k hk * fCl k hk) = A₂mul (affineSl2VOA_closed k hk) (eCl k hk) (fCl k hk)
        from rfl, A₂_leibniz, A₂bracket_f_e k hk, A₂bracket_self]
    change -hCl k hk * fCl k hk + eCl k hk * (0 : A₂ (affineSl2VOA_closed k hk))
      = (-1 : ℂ) • (hCl k hk * fCl k hk)
    rw [mul_zero, add_zero, neg_mul]
    module
  have hhh : A₂bracket (affineSl2VOA_closed k hk) (fCl k hk) (hCl k hk * hCl k hk)
      = (4 : ℂ) • (fCl k hk * hCl k hk) := by
    rw [show (hCl k hk * hCl k hk) = A₂mul (affineSl2VOA_closed k hk) (hCl k hk) (hCl k hk)
        from rfl, A₂_leibniz, A₂bracket_f_h k hk]
    change (2 : ℂ) • fCl k hk * hCl k hk + hCl k hk * ((2 : ℂ) • fCl k hk)
      = (4 : ℂ) • (fCl k hk * hCl k hk)
    rw [A₂_smul_mul, A₂_mul_smul, mul_comm (hCl k hk) (fCl k hk)]
    module
  rw [casimirCl, map_add, map_smul, hef, hhh, mul_comm (fCl k hk) (hCl k hk)]
  module

/-- `⁅[h], 4[e][f] + [h]²⁆ = 0`. -/
theorem A₂bracket_h_casimir :
    A₂bracket (affineSl2VOA_closed k hk) (hCl k hk) (casimirCl k hk) = 0 := by
  have hef : A₂bracket (affineSl2VOA_closed k hk) (hCl k hk) (eCl k hk * fCl k hk) = 0 := by
    rw [show (eCl k hk * fCl k hk) = A₂mul (affineSl2VOA_closed k hk) (eCl k hk) (fCl k hk)
        from rfl, A₂_leibniz, A₂bracket_h_e k hk, A₂bracket_h_f k hk]
    change (2 : ℂ) • eCl k hk * fCl k hk + eCl k hk * ((-2 : ℂ) • fCl k hk) = 0
    rw [A₂_smul_mul, A₂_mul_smul]
    module
  have hhh : A₂bracket (affineSl2VOA_closed k hk) (hCl k hk) (hCl k hk * hCl k hk) = 0 := by
    rw [show (hCl k hk * hCl k hk) = A₂mul (affineSl2VOA_closed k hk) (hCl k hk) (hCl k hk)
        from rfl, A₂_leibniz, A₂bracket_self]
    change (0 : A₂ (affineSl2VOA_closed k hk)) * hCl k hk
        + hCl k hk * (0 : A₂ (affineSl2VOA_closed k hk)) = 0
    rw [zero_mul, mul_zero, add_zero]
  rw [casimirCl, map_add, map_smul, hef, hhh, smul_zero, add_zero]

end VOA.Sl2Symbol

